    <h2>Comprehensive ExifTool CLI Flag Cheat Sheet and Web Equivalents</h2>
    <p>
      The table below maps common terminal ExifTool commands to RemoveSynth in-browser utilities:
    </p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Objective</th>
            <th>Terminal CLI Command (Phil Harvey)</th>
            <th>RemoveSynth In-Browser Equivalent</th>
            <th>Speed &amp; Privacy</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Wipe All Metadata</strong></td>
            <td><code>exiftool -all= image.jpg</code></td>
            <td>Click &quot;Strip All Metadata&quot; button above</td>
            <td>Instantaneous (&lt; 30ms) · Zero Uploads</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Remove GPS Only</strong></td>
            <td><code>exiftool -gps:all= image.jpg</code></td>
            <td><a href="/geotag-photo/">Geotag Photo Tool</a> (Wipe GPS)</td>
            <td>Instantaneous · Retains camera tags</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
